   "one_line": "About a third of the world's helium goes offline; Korean and Taiwanese fabs start rationing.",
   "summary": "Missile and drone strikes halted gas processing at Ras Laffan, which supplies roughly a third of the world's helium. Chip fabs need helium to cool and purge their tools, and the sample map shows TSMC, Samsung and SK hynix all depend on it. Because those three make most AI chips and most high-bandwidth memory, the shortage could travel on to Nvidia and AMD and then to the cloud companies building AI data centers. Industrial gas companies with helium from other sources, such as Linde and Air Products, may gain from higher prices. How bad it gets depends mostly on how much helium the fabs had stored, which the map does not know.",
